  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe makes 8"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "korokke"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "and takes around 1 hour in total. The filling is seasoned mashed potato with browned mince and onion, shaped into ovals, coated in flour, egg, and"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "panko"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", then deep-fried until golden. Serve with"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "tonkatsu sauce"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "for dipping."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The filling must be completely cold before you bread the korokke. If it is warm, the coating will slide off during frying and the croquettes will split open. Mash the potato until smooth and dry, with no lumps. Any excess moisture in the filling will cause the coating to burst in the oil. Chilling the shaped, breaded korokke on a tray for 20 minutes before frying helps them hold their shape."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
